\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JUNE 7, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer and Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Parker, Peirce, Steller, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Alex Farassati.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rThe City Council concurred to approve the agenda.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Councilmember Wolfson announced that members of the Spirit of Calabasas visited Plaquemines Parish, Louisiana, to assist in the rebuilding of a senior citizen center. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced the Calabasas Historical Society�s Annual Bar-B-Q on Sunday, June 11 at the Leonis Adobe. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian spoke regarding City events that will be occurring on the Fourth of July. Mayor Washburn announced that the Calabasas Library will be hosting special high school study hours, including free refreshments. Mayor Washburn spoke regarding an upcoming meeting of the Las Virgenes Council of Governments on June 19.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT: \r\r Esther Schiller, Thousand Oaks, and Steven Gallegos, Glendale, spoke in support of the City adopting an ordinance to restrict smoking in multi-unit housing, such as apartment buildings. Pamela Evans, Calabasas, spoke regarding traffic and safety concerns on Paul Revere Drive.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the May 24, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to approve the appointment of Michael Brockman by Councilmember Maurer to the Communications & Technology Commission, term ending March 31, 2007. \r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Item #1. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rCouncilmember Maurer introduced Michael Brockman, who she is appointing to the Communications & Technology Commission.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r \r Discussion on expanded polysterene ban. \r\rRobert Yalda, Public Works Director/City Engineer, Alex Farassatti, Environmental Services Manager, Jennifer Voccola, City of Malibu Environmental Programs Analyst, presented the staff report.\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, directed staff to conduct a survey of businesses and return to Council with a draft ordinance to eliminate the use of polysterene in the City. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Mayor Washburn voting NO.\r\r Fiscal Years 2006-07 and 2007-08 Budget Review. \r\rGary Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, presented the staff report.\r\rKeith Zajic, Calabasas, spoke in support of certain capital improvement projects that are proposed in the 2006-07 budget and expressed concern that the same amount of money was not allocated for capital improvement projects in the 2007-08 budget.\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve the 2006-07 and 2007-08 Budget. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING \r\r Waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2006-224, amending the User�s Guide and Chapter 22, Affordable Housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, as necessary to bring the City�s Density Bonus provisions into conformance with the affordable housing laws of the State of California. \r\rMayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\rTom Bartlett, City Planner, provided the staff report.\r\rMayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2006-224, amending the User�s Guide and Chapter 22, Affordable Housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, as necessary to bring the City�s Density Bonus provisions into conformance with the affordable housing laws of the State of California. MOTION CARRIED 3/2 with Mayor pro Tem Bozajian and Mayor Washburn voting NO. \r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1025, approving the Calabasas Creek Master Plan for restoration.\r\rAlex Farassatti, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rThe item was continued to the July 19, 2006 Council meeting. \r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of May 16, 2006 to May 25, 2006. \r\r No Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no Task Force Reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested an update on a proposed multi-unit housing smoking ban ordinance and the possibility of establishing a youth music program. \r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:30 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r06/07/06\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000r\b\u0000\u0000}\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0